#FUSSAREA
#AREADATA
Version      1
Name         Luna Complex~
Author       ZeroPoint~
Ranges       0 0 0 103
Economy      0 15000000
ResetMsg     A low vibration passes through the Luna Complex as life-support systems cycle.~
ResetFreq    15
Flags        nopkill~
#ENDAREADATA

#ROOM
Vnum     33000
Name     &CLuna Transfer Pad &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob can_land can_fly~
Desc     A reinforced landing pad occupies a level shelf cut into the lunar regolith.
Floodlights mark the docking collar while guidance beacons track approaching craft.
Pressure-rated service lines run beneath armored covers toward the terminal lock.
Beyond the safety barrier, the grey surface rolls toward a hard, airless horizon.
The terminal pressure lock stands east of the active pad.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33001
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33001
Name     &CTransfer Pressure Lock &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     A broad pressure lock separates the landing pad from the inhabited complex.
Status panels monitor atmosphere, suit seals and the position of both blast doors.
Dust-removal jets and floor grilles keep abrasive regolith outside the clean zone.
The landing pad lies west and the arrivals concourse opens east.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33000
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33002
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33002
Name     &CCentral Arrivals Concourse &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     The main concourse is built from pale pressure panels braced by exposed ribs.
Route displays list Earth transfers, habitat services and current surface conditions.
Cargo lanes are recessed into the floor so passengers can cross the compact hall safely.
Operations lies north, habitation east, medical services south and the transfer lock west.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33003
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33006
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33001
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33003
Name     &CComplex Operations &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     Controllers supervise docking, power allocation and environmental systems here.
A curved operations table carries a live diagram of the buried complex and surface pad.
Earth hangs above the local horizon on one wall display beside shuttle telemetry.
The concourse is south and the communications room is east.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33002
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33010
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33004
Name     &CHabitat Junction &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     Four pressure corridors meet beneath a circular emergency bulkhead assembly.
Soft lighting and planted wall modules temper the complex's functional construction.
Signs point west to arrivals, east to the commons, north to observation and south below.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33002
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33009
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33005
Name     &CHabitat Commons &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Tables, compact food dispensers and shared work booths fill the habitat commons.
The furniture is secured against vibration but arranged to give residents an open meeting place.
A local information wall carries duty rosters, Earth news and community notices.
The habitat junction is west and the clinic is south.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33006
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33006
Name     &CLuna Medical Clinic &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     A compact clinic provides routine care and emergency stabilization for the complex.
Two treatment couches face sealed cabinets stocked for decompression and radiation exposure.
Diagnostic equipment is mounted directly to the walls to keep the central aisle clear.
The arrivals concourse is north and the habitat commons is east.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33002
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33005
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33007
Name     &CRegolith Research Laboratory &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     Sealed benches hold mineral samples returned from nearby drilling sites.
Analysis cabinets test regolith chemistry while filtered transfer ports protect the habitat.
Survey maps mark extraction limits, buried ice prospects and protected scientific zones.
The subsurface access gallery is north.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33008
Name     &CSubsurface Access Gallery &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     A sloping gallery descends through exposed lunar rock beneath the habitat.
Utility conduits follow the walls toward laboratories and the shielded engineering level.
Emergency shelters are inset at regular intervals along the pressure-rated passage.
The habitat is north, the laboratory south and engineering access east.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33007
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33011
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33009
Name     &CEarth Observation Gallery &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     Layered radiation glass frames Earth above the stark lunar landscape.
Recessed seats face the window while navigation overlays identify orbital traffic.
The gallery remains dim so the blue-white planet and sunlit regolith dominate the view.
The habitat junction is south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33010
Name     &CCommunications Control &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     Directional arrays maintain continuous links with Earth and nearby orbital infrastructure.
Operators monitor shuttle clearances, emergency channels and delayed surface expeditions.
Shielded equipment racks surround a central communications console.
Complex operations lies west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33003
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33011
Name     &CEngineering Access &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     Heavy pressure doors divide the inhabited complex from its engineering spaces.
Coolant, power and atmosphere lines are color-coded across the reinforced ceiling.
Tool lockers and isolation controls stand ready beside each service branch.
The subsurface gallery is west and the power room is east.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33012
Name     &CFusion and Life-Support Plant &w:: &zLuna Complex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     The complex's power conversion and atmosphere systems operate behind armored partitions.
Status columns report reserve oxygen, water recovery, thermal load and reactor output.
The steady machinery hum is carried through the floor rather than the insulated walls.
The engineering access corridor returns west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33011
#ENDEXIT
#ENDROOM

#ENDAREA
